HOW TO READ THIS:
  return_pa   annualised return
  sharpe      return per unit of risk (>1 good, >2 excellent)
  maxDD       worst peak-to-trough loss
  R2          does signal STRENGTH predict return SIZE?
              0.00 = no, strength is a filter, not a dial
  corr / t    signed correlation of |strength| with trade R, and
              its t-stat (|t| > 2 ~ significant at 5%); n = trades
  Sharpe SE   Lo (2002), IID; Sharpe within 2 SE of 0 = not significant
  DSR         deflated Sharpe: probability the true Sharpe beats the
              best of N tries by luck (> 0.95 = significant)
  overfit     1.0 = edge fully survived on unseen data

